Subject: [PATCH 10/10] =?UTF-8?q?feat(settings):=20lead=20with=20=E4=B8=AD?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E6=96=87,=20and=20retire=20the=20two=20card-language=20pickers?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chinese moves to the front of the language list — presentation only, nothing
about resolution changes.

The CARD ART LANGUAGE and CARD TEXT LANGUAGE rows are removed. Both preferences
default to `"auto"`, so the interface picker alone now decides the cards: choose
Chinese and the cards are Chinese, choose English and they are English. One
control instead of three.

Removing the rows is not enough on its own, and this is the part that would have
bitten later: values written while those rows existed stay in storage and `merge`
restores them, so `artLanguage: "zhs"` would have gone on overriding the interface
language forever with nothing on screen able to change it. They are dropped from
`partialize` instead, which retires the stored values — "follow the interface"
becomes structural rather than a default stale state can defeat.

Also removes the flag switch's missing `zhs` arm, which is why Chinese had no
flag next to a `SupportedLng` that already listed it, and the constants, hooks, and
imports the deleted rows left behind.
